%
%  Configuration (v5):
%   - Boil-off line is ALWAYS OPEN to the Abgaskamin: 1" tube, Swagelok SS-1610
%     fitting, DN40/DN80 vent header. No boil-off valve -> tank sits at ~1 atm,
%     LH2 at ~20.3 K, boiling off continuously.
%   - TACOMA as built: NO safety valves, NO burst disc. Only pressure transmitters
%     (monitoring + alarm). The open vent is the ONLY relief path. Set has_SV = true
%     to see what two safety valves at MEOP would change.
%   - He purge as a flow-through (sweep) purge at ~1 atm; He leak test at 4 bar g
%     with the vent fitting CAPPED (warm tank only).
%   - Gas supply and vent per R&I 'Gasversorgung' (SVE, DN15 PN25, DN40/DN80 PN40).
%
%  STEPS / FIGURES
%   1-2  Geometry, LH2 property table
%   3    Pressure levels & burst                        -> Fig 1
%   4    He purge + leak-test limits                    -> Fig 2
%   5    LN2 / LH2 chilldown                            -> Fig 3
%   6    LH2 capacity + fill height                     -> Fig 4
%   7    Heat leak
%   8    HYDROS check, open-vent boil-off, blocked vent -> Fig 5, Fig 9
%   10   He leak-test pressurisation + blowdown         -> Fig 6
%   11   Open vent capacity + safety valves             -> Fig 7
%   12   Measured logger data (or DEMO) vs model        -> Fig 8
%   13   Summary
%  Pressures in Pa ABSOLUTE unless the name ends in _g (gauge).
%  Lines marked  % <-- PLACEHOLDER / % <-- CHECK  need real values.
%  MATLAB R2020b or newer (local functions at the end of the script).
%% ========================================================================
